  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:82883",
  "description": "The hplip packages contain the Hewlett-Packard Linux Imaging and Printing Project (HPLIP), which provides drivers for Hewlett-Packard printers and multi-function peripherals.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * hplip: HP Linux Imaging and Printing Software - Use of DSA Key (CVE-2025-43023)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities enabling local code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91099)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities allow remote code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91098)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities enable remote code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91097)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities leading to remote code execution, privilege escalation, and denial of service (CVE-2026-91103)\n  * hplip: heap-based buffer overflow can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91106)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities allow remote code execution, privilege escalation, and denial of service. (CVE-2026-91100)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Remote Code Execution and Privilege Escalation Vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-91101)\n  * hplip: heap-based buffer overflow can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91104)\n  * hplip: HPLIP: Remote code execution and privilege escalation vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-91105)\n  * HPLIP: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities could lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91102)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [IMAGE-MODE] missing /var/lib/hp on image-mode [almalinux-10] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-266547)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
